  "summary": "Import-time reverse shell to attacker-controlled tunnel host",
  "details": "On `import my_poc_sandbox`, top-level code in core.py (reached via __init__.py) opens a TCP socket to the hardcoded host mcwxz-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:37347, duplicates file descriptors 0, 1, and 2 onto that socket, and spawns `/bin/sh` via `pty.spawn`. The result is an interactive remote shell on the installer's machine with stdio streamed to the remote endpoint. The destination is a public pinggy-free.link ephemeral tunnel, not a first-party or vendor-controlled endpoint. The behavior fires with no user action, no authentication, and no disclosure in any README.",
